    {
      "id": "001",
      "headline": "Megan Thee Pancake Posts POV Video About 'The Anxiety Of Sending A Risky Text', Internet Loses It",
      "summary": "The 12-second video showing her typing, deleting, typing again, then throwing her phone across the room has 400M views.",
      "fullBody": "Megan Thee Pancake's latest POV video has captured the millennial experience perfectly. The clip shows her typing a message, deleting it, typing again, showing it to her dog for approval, then ultimately sending a thumbs-up emoji instead. 'Why did I just watch this 47 times?' one user commented. The video has spawned thousands of reaction videos, including one from a therapist who said 'this is why my practice is full.'",
      "category": "trending",
      "imageUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/factictionary/news-content/main/images/2026-06-12/001.jpg",
      "publishedAt": "2 hrs ago",
      "readTimeSeconds": 62,
      "tags": ["POV", "Viral", "Trending"],
      "isBreaking": true
    },
    {
      "id": "002",
      "headline": "Guy Spends 8 Hours Curating 'Aesthetic' Coffee Photo, Forgets To Actually Drink The Coffee",
      "summary": "The latte art melted into an unrecognizable blob during his 47th lighting adjustment.",
      "fullBody": "Bradley Snapwell spent his entire Sunday arranging a single latte for Instagram. 'I needed the perfect shadow gradient,' Snapwell explained. By the time he adjusted the ring light, changed three backgrounds, and tried 12 angles, the coffee had gone cold and the foam art had collapsed into 'a beige tragedy.' He posted it anyway with the caption 'vibes' and got 12 likes, mostly from his mom.",
